{"beat": 2, "name": "LET THEM BE WRONG", "text": "Here's the test most of us run. Pick a product. Raise the price a notch. Watch it for a few weeks. Compare units and revenue to the weeks before. If revenue went up and units held, keep the new price. If units fell away, put it back. It's a fair test. It's what every pricing tool suggests, and it feels like evidence because something measurable happened. The problem isn't the idea of testing. The problem is how much a few weeks can tell you, and it's far less than it looks.", "provider": "library", "words": [{"word": "Here's", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.267}, {"word": "the", "start": 0.29, "end": 0.36}, {"word": "test", "start": 0.395, "end": 0.627}, {"word": "most", "start": 0.685, "end": 0.882}, {"word": "of", "start": 0.917, "end": 0.964}, {"word": "us", "start": 1.022, "end": 1.103}, {"word": "run.", "start": 1.173, "end": 1.649}, {"word": "Pick", "start": 2.032, "end": 2.229}, {"word": "a", "start": 2.264, "end": 2.287}, {"word": "product.", "start": 2.322, "end": 2.995}, {"word": "Raise", "start": 3.379, "end": 3.75}, {"word": "the", "start": 3.785, "end": 3.855}, {"word": "price", "start": 3.913, "end": 4.214}, {"word": "a", "start": 4.249, "end": 4.272}, {"word": "notch.", "start": 4.354, "end": 4.946}, {"word": "Watch", "start": 5.271, "end": 5.584}, {"word": "it", "start": 5.642, "end": 5.7}, {"word": "for", "start": 5.747, "end": 5.863}, {"word": "a", "start": 5.921, "end": 5.944}, {"word": "few", "start": 5.991, "end": 6.153}, {"word": "weeks.", "start": 6.2, "end": 6.745}, {"word": "Compare", "start": 6.861, "end": 7.279}, {"word": "units", "start": 7.372, "end": 7.697}, {"word": "and", "start": 7.755, "end": 7.86}, {"word": "revenue", "start": 7.93, "end": 8.44}, {"word": "to", "start": 8.522, "end": 8.649}, {"word": "the", "start": 8.707, "end": 8.777}, {"word": "weeks", "start": 8.847, "end": 9.125}, {"word": "before.", "start": 9.183, "end": 9.892}, {"word": "If", "start": 10.217, "end": 10.379}, {"word"